@tradition talent-night
// Talent night: once a year (the user, check-in A), day 152, a Friday in Greening, in the bow lounge; on the night it
// takes the music jam's place (the voice budget: the rarer wins). Musicians and anyone brave.
// The seat 16 designer's (claude/trad-monthly). Notes: plans/trad-notes-monthly.md. Format: plans/trad-format.md.
k: 455
title: Talent night
when: year day 152
at: 20:15-21:45
min: 25
jitter: 20
where: 3 room Bow lounge: lounge-seat
who: dahl-mira always, musician 85%, music 55%, lounge-regular 50%, bar-regular 45%, everyone 25%
anim: musician play, bar-regular drink, everyone talk
host: dahl-mira
from: dahl-mira
ties: decor talentStage
invite: host=dahl-mira odds=35% line="Talent night tonight. You don't have to get up. But you could."

== mail
- Talent night tomorrow, {time} in the bow lounge. Sing, play, juggle, read a poem, or just clap loudly. Sign up at the bar.

== ask
- Talent night later. I'm doing a card trick. It works about half the time.   #funny
- Are you coming to talent night? Somebody has to clap.
- I've practised my song in the shower all week. Ask anyone in my bunk room.   #funny

== here
- Give them a big hand!
- Next up, someone very brave.   #funny
- Shh, this one's lovely.   #warm

== thanks
- You find a seat for talent night. Every act gets a cheer, even the one that goes wrong.   #warm

== chatter
- Who's on first at talent night? Not me. Never me.   #funny
- Mira says anyone can do talent night. Even a talk about bolts.   #funny
- Last talent night, someone played a tune on the water pipes.
- I clapped so hard at talent night my hands hurt.   #warm
